  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` to `src/cli/truncate.ts` and committed it as `ea8b0ba`. The new tests pass, and `npm run fast` passes.\n\n- **Behaviour:** Text that already fits in `max` comes back unchanged. Longer text keeps both ends around a single `…`, and the result is exactly `max` characters long. When the kept characters can't split evenly, the start gets the extra one. A limit of 1 returns `…`, and a limit of 0 or less returns an empty string.\n- **Emoji:** It counts whole characters, so it won't split an emoji in the middle.\n- **Tests:** The tests are in `test/cli/truncate.test.ts` and cover unchanged text, both ends kept, the tiny limits, and emoji.\n- **Shard weight:** I gave the new test file a weight of 0.1 in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`, as the repo conventions require.\n\nThe commit title ends with `(t-7osxd0r)`. I didn't touch the task tracker.",
